FILE-15: do not skip the previous link in the parser's valve check

valvecheck() skips the valve whose link index it is given, so that a
valve being edited is not compared with itself. valvedata() calls it
while reading a new valve, before the valve is added, and passed
net->Nlinks, which is the index of the link read before it. When
that link is also a valve, the pair was never checked, so for example
two PRVs on consecutive lines could share a downstream node. The new
valve has no index yet, so pass 0, as EN_addlink does.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-15_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/input3.c b/src/input3.c
index e97110f..80c7a85 100644
--- a/src/input3.c
+++ b/src/input3.c
@@ -599,7 +599,7 @@ int valvedata(Project *pr)
     else return setError(parser, 4, 213);
     
     // Check for illegal connections
-    if (valvecheck(pr, net->Nlinks, type, j1, j2))
+    if (valvecheck(pr, 0, type, j1, j2))
     {
         if      (j1 > net->Njuncs) return setError(parser, 1, 219);
         else if (j2 > net->Njuncs) return setError(parser, 2, 219);
